---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import SocialGateway from '../components/SocialGateway.astro';
import { site, url } from '../data/site';
import { expertise } from '../data/expertise';

const { owner } = site;
---

<Layout
  title={`Meet ${owner.name}`}
  description={`${owner.name}, ${owner.role} at ${site.name}. One point of contact from quote to completion, with in-depth knowledge of UK Building Regulations.`}
>
  <div class="placeholder">
    <strong>Draft page.</strong> Text in yellow boxes and anything marked [like this] needs details from Ashley.
  </div>

  <section class="profile-hero">
    <div class="profile-photo">
      [Photo of Ashley on site: a real photo in work gear, not a studio headshot]
    </div>
    <div>
      <h1 class="page-title">Meet {owner.name}</h1>
      <div class="profile-role">{owner.role}</div>
      <p class="lead">
        When you hire AJH, you get Ashley. He prices your job, builds it with his team and runs the project day to day,
        so the person who made you promises at the quote is the one on site keeping them.
      </p>
      <p>
        [Placeholder: a few lines on Ashley's background. How he got into the trade, when he started AJH,
        the kind of projects he enjoys most, and what he's proudest of.]
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-whatsapp" href={site.whatsappHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><Icon name="whatsapp" size={18} /> WhatsApp Ashley</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href={site.phoneHref}><Icon name="phone" size={16} /> {site.phone}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2 class="dash-heading">One person, three roles</h2>
  <div class="hats">
    <div class="hat">
      <h4>Owner</h4>
      <p>Your quote comes straight from the person accountable for it. No sales team, no surprises.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hat">
      <h4>Head builder</h4>
      <p>Ashley is hands-on at the build, not managing from an office, so standards stay consistent.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hat">
      <h4>Project manager</h4>
      <p>He books the trades, supervises deliveries and handles Building Control, and you have one number to call.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="dash-heading">Knows the “why”, not just the “how”</h2>
  <p>
    Any builder can follow a drawing. Ashley knows the UK Building Regulations behind it: why a steel is sized the way
    it is, why a loft needs a protected escape route, why insulation has to hit a certain level. That means fewer
    surprises at inspection, and clear answers when you ask “do we really need that?”
  </p>
  <div class="placeholder">Draft examples below. Ashley to check wording and add his own.</div>
  <div class="why-grid">
    {expertise.map((e) => (
      <div class="why-card">
        <h4>{e.title}</h4>
        <div class="reg">{e.reg}</div>
        <p>{e.text}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <blockquote class="pull-quote">
    “[Placeholder: a line from Ashley in his own words, e.g. why he explains the regs to clients rather than just building to them.]”
  </blockquote>

  <h2 class="dash-heading">Experience & credentials</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    <li>Building in and around Hertfordshire since 2000</li>
    <li>[Placeholder: trade qualifications, e.g. NVQ / CSCS card level]</li>
    <li>[Placeholder: trade memberships, e.g. FMB, TrustMark]</li>
    <li>[Placeholder: insurance, e.g. public liability cover amount]</li>
    <li>[Placeholder: guarantees offered on work]</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Want to see his work first? Take a look at <a href={url('/current-projects/')}>current projects</a> or
    <a href={site.google} target="_blank" rel="noopener">read his reviews on Google</a>. Past clients
    are also happy to show you their finished builds.
  </p>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <SocialGateway heading={`Follow ${owner.firstName}'s latest builds`} />
</Layout>
